.TH VSNPRINTF 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
vsnprintf \- format a System V argument list into a bounded byte buffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "int vsnprintf(char *" buffer ", size_t " capacity ", const char *" format ,
.BI "              struct __crunch_va_list_tag *" arguments ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Formats an existing Linux x86-64 System V argument list into a bounded buffer.
It consumes the argument list, and supports the conversions documented in
.BR snprintf (3crunch)
and the additional string precision
.BR %.*s .
The destination and capacity rules are the same as for
.BR snprintf (3crunch).
Arguments and their types must match the format string.
.PP
Argument lists may be created using
.B stdarg.h
or supplied by interoperating C code.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of bytes that would have been written, excluding the
terminating NUL, or \-1 on error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR snprintf (3crunch)
